  "wikitext": "{{PageDisplay}}\n[[File:Nectar Bush.png|left|200px|Nectar bush]]\n\n{{Infobox\n |level = 39|price = 120|time = every ?|xp = 5|dia = ?|title = [[Trees and Bushes|Trees & bushes]]|gives = nectar}}\n'''Nectar bushes''' are a type of [[Trees and Bushes|bush]] unlocked at [[experience]] level 39.\n\nEach bush can give up to 500 drops of nectar, which are collected in 2 harvests.\n\n{{Clr}}\n----\n==='''Stages'''===\n{| style=\"text-align: center;\"\n|-\n|[[File:Nectar Bush.png|left|100px]]\n|[[File:Nectar Bush Stage 2.png|left|100px]]\n|-\n|'''Ready'''\n|'''Dead'''\n|}\n----\n==='''Buying'''===\n{{Infoicon|shop|bigger|link=Shop}} Nectar bushes can be purchased in the [[shop]] for 120 [[coin]]s each.\n----\n==='''Harvesting'''===\nThere is no growth cycle for nectar bushes. Each bush contains 250 drops of nectar and can be continuously harvested.\n----\n==='''Revival'''===\n[[File:Nectar Bush Revival.png|left|150px]]\nOnce its nectar has been depleted, the bush wilts. A player can ask for another player to revive it by tapping on it and placing a sign on the bush. When another player revives it a final harvest of 250 drops of nectar can be collected before the bush dies.  The helper gets 8 {{Infoicon|xp}} points for reviving the nectar bush.\n\n{{Clr}}\n----\n==='''Removing'''===\n[[File:Axe.png|150px|left|An axe]]\nA [[axe]] is needed to remove a dead bush from the farm. Note that players may also use an axe to remove the bush after the first harvest instead of placing it up for revival.\n\n{{Clr}}\n----\n==='''Storing'''===\nNectar can never be directly collected or stored by the player. It goes automatically into the beehive on the [[Beehive Tree|beehive tree]].\n\nWhen the player is playing, the further the bush is from the beehive tree the longer it takes the bees to bring it to the beehive. When the player is offline, distance no longer matters.\n----\n\n{{Navigation}}\n{{Languages\n|de = Nektarbusch\n|es = Arbusto de néctar\n|fr = Fleurs à nectar\n|it = Cespuglio Di Nettare\n}}\n[[Category:Trees and Bushes]]",
